From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: report QC chargers as a DCP on liuqin

The SM8475 usb_type is USB_ADAP_TYPE, which extends power_supply_usb_type
with the QTI dedicated-charger types from 0x80. The class cannot name
them: with a QC charger, reading usb_type fails with -EINVAL, every read
and every change uevent logs "driver reporting unavailable enum value",
and the uevent goes out without POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE.

Report them the way stock battery_chg_update_usb_type_work() supplies them:
HVDCP, HVDCP_3 and HVDCP_3P5 as a DCP, and HVDCP_3 class B of the same
family too. A floating charger and any other value the class cannot name
read as unknown, as in stock's default case. The raw type still drives the
charging wakeup source and the input current limit.

KUnit reads usb_type through a registered power supply's sysfs attribute
and its uevent for each type; without the mapping both fail for 0x80-0x84.
The test uses the power supply class internals, so it is built-in only.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Liuqin-upstream: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/commit/c25f056e0c20e7a9fd0632598909568005fdfc56

Liuqin Fedora port: adopt reporting independently of the upstream 500 mA input policy, with no added write interface.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -95,6 +95,11 @@
 #define USB_CURR_MAX			4
 #define USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT		5
 #define USB_TYPE			6
+#define SM8475_USB_ADAP_HVDCP		0x80
+#define SM8475_USB_ADAP_HVDCP_3		0x81
+#define SM8475_USB_ADAP_HVDCP_3P5	0x82
+#define SM8475_USB_ADAP_HVDCP_3_CLASSB	0x84
+
 #define USB_ADAP_TYPE			7
 #define USB_MOISTURE_DET_EN		8
 #define USB_MOISTURE_DET_STS		9
@@ -1813,6 +1818,28 @@
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The class only knows the power_supply_usb_type values, and SM8475 also
+ * reports the QTI dedicated-charger types from 0x80. Stock
+ * battery_chg_update_usb_type_work() supplies HVDCP, HVDCP_3 and HVDCP_3P5
+ * as a DCP; HVDCP_3 class B is the same QC charger family. Any other value is
+ * unknown, as in stock's default case, so reading usb_type never fails.
+ */
+static int qcom_battmgr_sm8475_usb_type(u32 type)
+{
+	switch (type) {
+	case SM8475_USB_ADAP_HVDCP:
+	case SM8475_USB_ADAP_HVDCP_3:
+	case SM8475_USB_ADAP_HVDCP_3P5:
+	case SM8475_USB_ADAP_HVDCP_3_CLASSB:
+		return POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_DCP;
+	}
+
+	/* Up to the Apple brick ID the firmware uses the class numbering. */
+	return type <= POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_APPLE_BRICK_ID ? type :
+	       POWER_SUPPLY_USB_TYPE_UNKNOWN;
+}
+
 static int qcom_battmgr_usb_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 					 enum power_supply_property psp,
 					 union power_supply_propval *val)
@@ -1852,6 +1879,8 @@
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_USB_TYPE:
 		val->intval = battmgr->usb.usb_type;
+		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8475)
+			val->intval = qcom_battmgr_sm8475_usb_type(val->intval);
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EINVAL;
